WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.640
- You literally are just back
from your honeymoon, right?

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:03.870
- Yes.
- Congratulations,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.862
on getting married.

00:00:04.862 --> 00:00:05.695
- Thank you.

00:00:05.695 --> 00:00:06.528
(audience applauds)

00:00:06.528 --> 00:00:07.361
- [Kelly] That's awesome.

00:00:07.361 --> 00:00:08.760
How was the honeymoon?

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.720
Oh my God.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.608
- Look at that.

00:00:10.608 --> 00:00:11.820
Look at that beautiful Ralph Lauren suit.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:12.653
Thank you.

00:00:12.653 --> 00:00:14.520
- Yeah, look at that dress.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:15.780
I'm sorry, I wasn't looking at you.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.528
Yeah, I was like, she looks beautiful.

00:00:18.528 --> 00:00:21.000
- She is. She is a little sweetheart.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.124
And we had an amazing time in Thailand.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:25.107
- Had you ever been?
- Have you ever been?

00:00:25.107 --> 00:00:26.700
- I have been to Thailand a few times.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.640
- Well it takes you about a
full 24 hours to get there.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:30.473
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:30.473 --> 00:00:31.306
- So it took us a day or two

00:00:31.306 --> 00:00:32.640
just to get acclimated to the time.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.180
But we went to this beautiful
resort called San Ava

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.620
on this little island in Thailand

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.670
for about four or five days.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.800
And then we went to Bangkok,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.200
which is a complete
- Totally different.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.020
- departure from the serenity of San Ava.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.220
- Yeah. is it true that you had to go

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.053
to the emergency room,

00:00:48.053 --> 00:00:49.632
like right before the wedding?
- I did.

00:00:49.632 --> 00:00:50.465
- That's a good start.

00:00:50.465 --> 00:00:52.410
- Well, yeah. Tell me about it.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.243
- Yeah.

00:00:53.243 --> 00:00:55.170
So it was like, we had this amazing band

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.300
play for the rehearsal
dinner the night before.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.133
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:02.430
- And we had a blast and afterwards

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.560
we went into the party bus
to go back to the hotel

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:05.820
and we had music pumping in there

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.200
and I'm feeling good.
- Feeling good.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.850
- So I decided I'm gonna start dancing.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.430
And they have those
handles that you hold on

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:12.263
in the party bus,
- To let loose.

00:01:12.263 --> 00:01:13.096
try to do this thing

00:01:13.096 --> 00:01:15.570
where you like like a gymnast,
like straighten myself out.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:16.560
And I was like, Oh!"

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.030
- Cause we have really good ideas read it.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.860
- Something just happened.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.870
And so, yeah. I felt fun.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:24.030
I got through that night and
I wake up the next morning

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.310
two hours before the wedding

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.350
and I couldn't get out of bed.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.640
I literally couldn't stand up,

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:30.960
so I was like what am I gonna do?

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:31.793
Oh my God.

00:01:31.793 --> 00:01:33.360
So they had to take me
to the emergency room,

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.780
give me a bunch of meds and
shoot me with toradol and...

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.613
- Oh my God.

00:01:37.613 --> 00:01:38.446
- And it was great.

00:01:38.446 --> 00:01:39.630
Everything went great.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:40.740
I got through the night,
- Of course it was,

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:41.880
You're on toradol

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:45.960
- Dance the night away next
morning after the wedding,

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.340
couldn't get out bed again.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.173
- [Kelly] Oh no.

00:01:48.173 --> 00:01:49.006
- They had to take me

00:01:49.006 --> 00:01:50.190
to the emergency room again the next night

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.170
and she's like, "Oh my God,
everything's fine here.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.730
This is like the first day of my marriage.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.160
And I'm wheeling my husband
around in a wheelchair."

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.320
I'm already old, way older than she is.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.710
So it wasn't a great start,
- But funny one,

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:02.580
- But,
- memorable.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:04.380
- I was like, Babe, for better or worse.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.643
- Yeah. You said so, I heard it.

